! ============================================================
! Passive/SPAN deployment shape. Traffic evidence for this shape comes
! from a tap or SPAN port lower in the Purdue stack (e.g. a Claroty
! style sensor) and is visibility only -- it does not enforce anything.
! The actual policy governing what's allowed lives separately, on the
! Level 3 core switch's own ACLs, a traditional networking vendor
! (Cisco IOS here) rather than the DMZ inline appliance.
! Cisco IOS extended named ACL syntax (distinct from the ASA syntax
! used for the inline appliance policy, since these are genuinely
! different devices from different vendors in this deployment shape).
! ============================================================

ip access-list extended CORE-SWITCH-ACL
 remark -- Site Ops (L3) to Area segments (L2-1): SCADA polling + eng access --
 permit tcp host 10.30.0.10 10.12.0.0 0.0.0.255 eq 502
 permit tcp host 10.30.0.10 10.13.0.0 0.0.0.255 eq 502
 permit tcp host 10.30.0.10 10.14.0.0 0.0.0.255 eq 502
 permit tcp host 10.30.0.10 10.15.0.0 0.0.0.255 eq 502
 permit tcp host 10.30.0.12 10.12.0.0 0.0.0.255 eq 502
 permit tcp host 10.30.0.12 10.13.0.0 0.0.0.255 eq 502
 permit tcp host 10.30.0.12 10.14.0.0 0.0.0.255 eq 502
 permit tcp host 10.30.0.12 10.15.0.0 0.0.0.255 eq 502
 remark -- Area to Area: deny by default --
 deny ip 10.12.0.0 0.0.0.255 10.13.0.0 0.0.0.255 log
 deny ip 10.12.0.0 0.0.0.255 10.14.0.0 0.0.0.255 log
 deny ip 10.12.0.0 0.0.0.255 10.15.0.0 0.0.0.255 log
 deny ip 10.13.0.0 0.0.0.255 10.14.0.0 0.0.0.255 log
 deny ip 10.13.0.0 0.0.0.255 10.15.0.0 0.0.0.255 log
 deny ip 10.14.0.0 0.0.0.255 10.15.0.0 0.0.0.255 log
 deny ip any any log
